# DR-0017: Materialize and Verify Image-Mask Pairs Before Dataset Splitting

## Status

Accepted

## Context

After deterministic sampling, Loop 1 has an ordered selection of 50 supervised candidate tiles.

Training requires physical image and mask artifacts, but writing files alone is insufficient. The project must be able to prove that every pair:

- corresponds to one selected candidate
- uses the approved source image and label raster
- preserves the candidate pixel window
- preserves spatial metadata
- preserves label values and counts
- remains linked to sampling and provenance identities

Spatial train-validation-test assignment occurs later. Physical pair generation must not silently assign subsets or change the selected population.

## Decision

Loop 1 materializes one physical GeoTIFF image tile and one physical GeoTIFF mask tile for every selected candidate before spatial split assignment.

The materialized population is:

```text
total image-mask pairs: 50
positive pairs: 19
negative-only pairs: 31
all-ignore pairs: 0
```

The source image properties are preserved:

```text
bands per image tile: 4
image dtype: float64 for every band
```

Mask artifacts use:

```text
bands per mask tile: 1
mask dtype: uint8
mask nodata: 255
allowed values: 0, 1, 255
```

