## Verification

Every physical pair is verified against the approved source rasters and its selected candidate record.

Verification covers:

```text
file existence and readability
image and mask dimensions
image band count and dtypes
mask band count, dtype, nodata, and allowed values
CRS equality
affine-transform equality
exact image-window pixel content
exact mask-window pixel content
positive pixel count
negative pixel count
ignore pixel count
label class
```

Real verification result:

```text
generated pairs: 50
verified pairs: 50
verification errors: 0
```

## Split Boundary

Pair generation does not assign training, validation, or test membership.

The later spatial-splitting phase will reference stable pair and tile identities.

This preserves the boundary:

```text
deterministic materialization
before
spatial subset assignment
```

Physical generation must not be rerun independently with different window logic for each subset.

## Consequences

Positive consequences:

- training inputs are concrete and inspectable before splitting
- every pair is traceable to source rasters, a candidate tile, a selection, and provenance
- physical corruption or incorrect windows are detected before model training
- later split manifests can reference stable pair identities
- repeated workflows can compare pair catalogs semantically

Trade-offs:

- materialization duplicates source raster pixels on disk
- overlapping tiles duplicate some image and label content
- GeoTIFF output size is larger than an on-demand window reader
- physical artifacts require storage and lifecycle management outside Git

These trade-offs are accepted for Loop 1 because explicit, verifiable artifacts provide a stronger dataset-release boundary.

## Alternatives Considered

### Read Source Windows Only at Training Time

Rejected for Loop 1 because it would defer physical verification and make the training package depend on runtime window extraction.

### Generate Files Separately for Each Dataset Split

Rejected because it could introduce inconsistent materialization logic and duplicate the selection boundary.

### Persist Only File Paths Without Pixel Verification

Rejected because path existence does not prove correct spatial or pixel content.

### Include All-Ignore Pairs

Rejected because all-ignore candidates are ineligible for supervised Loop 1 sampling.

